**brma class**
missing features
  - radial	Radial (Galbraith) plot
  - baujat	Baujat plot
  - qqnorm	QQ-normal plot
  - nobs	Number of observations
  - gosh	GOSH analysis
  - regplot	Regression/bubble plot
  - vif 	Variance inflation factors
  - robust	Cluster-robust inference

missing basic methods
  - coef	Extract model coefficients
  - vcov	Variance-covariance matrix of coefficients

missing wrappers:
  - confint	Confidence/credible intervals
  - fitted	Fitted values (currently only via predict)
  - ranef	Extract random effects

Other
- restrict I^2/H^2 output
- verify hatvalues calculation (sometimes bit of from metafor)


plot_weightfunction
Expand the function to use `show_data` argument. if TRUE, the function should show p-values as jitter on the x-axis
- compute p-values by transformation of yi/sei
- note that re-scale options spaces the cutpoints equally (not mapping to p-values directly)
- note that two-sided only weightfunction with bselmodel use two sided p-values, other use one-sided p-values
